    deepExplanation: "Execution flow: The application invokes or triggers **Dedicated Worker**. → The browser validates the relevant document, origin, permission or lifecycle state. → The responsible browser subsystem performs the operation. → The result is delivered synchronously or through an asynchronous callback/event. → Any DOM, network, storage, rendering or memory consequences become observable.\n\nProduction pattern:\n\n```js\n// Production rule for Dedicated Worker: isolate the capability behind a small boundary.\nexport function useBrowserCapability() {\n  if (typeof window === \"undefined\") return false;\n  return true;\n}\n```\n\nExpected output:\n\n```text\nWorker output is asynchronous and depends on the worker message handler.\n```\n\nPerformance: Avoid unnecessary main-thread work. Measure before optimizing with Performance, Network and Memory tooling. Batch DOM reads/writes when layout work is involved. Use caching, streaming, lazy loading and resource hints when they match the workload. Consider memory retention and cleanup for listeners, observers, workers and long-lived resources.\n\nSecurity: Respect the Same-Origin Policy, CORS, CSP, secure contexts, permissions, cookie attributes and iframe isolation. Never treat client-side checks as a replacement for server authorization.",
